Prepare this host's context-independent controller prerequisites: the baseline host packages, installed through the host's own dnf, and the controller runtime, a venv on the OS Python holding exactly the wheels this build locks. Setup selects no context; the prerequisites a context adds are installed by the controller stage of apply. A ready host makes no request and no change. Otherwise the plan shows dnf's own preview before confirmation. --dry-run never elevates: it names the host package requirements without a preview and makes no changes, and --output json, accepted only with --dry-run, also lists every locked wheel's file, URL and SHA-256. Review the plan before confirming; --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

Usage:
  bootwright setup [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright setup --dry-run

Flags:
      --dry-run         Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --output string   Select output mode (values: text, json) (default "text")
      --yes             Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

Global Flags:
      --context string             Ignored: setup selects no context
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
